# Dagger of Wounding: a magic variant of any dagger (Deep Magic 12).
ITEMS = []; SP = {}; WPN = {}; GEAR = []
ITEMS.append(("Dagger of Wounding (*)", "Weapon", "Rare", 1,
 "Any dagger can become a Dagger of Wounding. Hit points lost to its damage return only through a short or long rest, not through regeneration, magic, or any other means. Once per turn, when you hit a creature with an attack using it, you can wound the target. At the start of each of the wounded creature's turns, it takes 1d4 necrotic damage for each time you wounded it, then makes a DC 15 Constitution saving throw. A success ends all such wounds on it. A wounded creature, or a creature within 5 feet of it, can instead use an action to make a DC 15 Wisdom (Medicine) check. A success ends the wounds.", {}))
